cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, you may cite it — but CC0 requires nothing of you."
title: "substrate-phycom: seed-expander connective layer"
abstract: >-
  A connective layer that makes the EXPANDER pluggable in seed-based
  physics communication. You transmit a 120-bit seed, not the message; a
  shared deterministic physics model, which never crosses the wire,
  expands it. The model is simultaneously the compression and the access
  gate. Includes a terrestrial geomagnetic field-model expander, so the
  architecture runs with no orbital dependency, and a ledger of every
  claim the project has made, tested, and falsified.
